# .recur-watch

Purpose: describe the watcher capability split between the read-only core query
surface and the active watcher runner.

What it offers today:

- `recur watch` reads watcher ACK/NAK state under `.recur/watch/` and exits.
- `recur-watch` is the active runner that can observe eventness files.
- `recur capability explain watch` can show this card before an operator uses
  either surface.

Current boundary:

- Core `recur watch` is query-only.
- Active watching belongs to the companion runner.
- Capability cards are project knowledge; they do not start processes.

Trace-id lines:

```text
defines: recur.watch.capability live filesystem eventness stream and watcher-state query surface
consumes: main.improvement.28 recur capability-card query surface for root .recur-* files
produces: recur.watch.readiness shared card describing query runner and state-file boundaries
triggers: recur.capability.doctor verify watch capability card presence
```